--- a/drivers/power/supply/rk818_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk818_battery.c
@@ -7,28 +7,35 @@
  * Design:
  * - Coulomb counter is the primary SoC source; it is accurate when
  *   COFFSET is correctly calibrated.
- * - OCV (open-circuit voltage) and relaxed voltage are used to
- *   periodically re-anchor the coulomb counter.
+ * - The counter runs on through power-offs and counts a charge in U-Boot's
+ *   wait (rk818_init_soc()); the OCV (open-circuit voltage) re-anchors it
+ *   after a rest: at a power-on after OCV_LEVEL_REST_MIN off or at the end
+ *   of a cycle, at a wake after REST_SLEEP_MIN asleep off the charger. Not
+ *   the PMIC's relaxed voltage (rk818_update_soc()).
  * - Display SoC (dsoc) tracks real SoC (rsoc) through a simple
  *   rate-limiter so it never jumps more than 1% per poll cycle.
  * - At charge completion the coulomb counter is snapped to FCC.
- * - COFFSET auto-calibration runs once per charge cycle when the
- *   charger reports RK818_CHG_STS_TERMINATED and current appears near zero.
+ * - The zero of the current (COFFSET) comes from a charge balance over
+ *   ends of a charge (rk818_balance()); an end-of-charge calibration is the
+ *   first estimate only (rk818_auto_calib_coffset()).
  */
 
